the seven warlords of the sea?

259
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:56,197
Didn't I just say that?

260
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:58,437
In any case, you're
obviously not a threat to me,

261
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:00,077
so let's get to know
each other personally.

262
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:01,100
I'll start.

263
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:04,137
Did you know I haven't had
my haircut in my entire life?

264
00:16:04,220 --> 00:16:05,620
That's over 25 years.

265
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:08,160
You're impressed and jealous. Admit it.

266
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,340
That's lame.

267
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:11,400
How dare you?

268
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:12,817
Watch your mouth, kid.

269
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:14,697
Settle down, my faithful divers.

270
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:18,757
I'm not gonna let these foul-mouthed
punks get away with insulting me.

271
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,120
Take this to heart.

272
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:23,437
Sail through the tunnel that
is my rage and you'll be

273
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:26,638
met by a sea of blood from
which you'll never escape.

274
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:29,400
Yeah, whatever. Move aside.

275
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:31,717
We have places to go and people to meet.

276
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:33,565
You just don't get it, do you?

277
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:37,837
This is my turf, and if you want to
pass, you either pay the toll or be sunk.

278
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:38,750
Get it?

279
00:16:38,833 --> 00:16:40,397
What's this guy mean by his turf?

280
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:42,697
He's starting to sound like
our old friend Mashida.

281
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:43,610
Huh?

282
00:16:43,693 --> 00:16:45,157
Mashida said stuff like that?

283
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:46,180
What? Mashida?

284
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:47,840
What about Mashida?

285
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:52,657
If you must know, we kicked his butt
off our boat, but we didn't think...

286
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:53,570
You what?

287
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:54,700
Kicked him?

288
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:55,900
Easy, boss.

289
00:16:57,220 --> 00:17:01,157
How dare you lay a hand on my
brother, my own flesh and blood!

290
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:04,358
Sure we threw him off our
boat, but I bet he's alive.

291
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:08,560
Havoc sonar!

292
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:27,280
The ship!

293
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:34,880
So, what are they doing?

294
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:38,060
Who knows, but it's amazing.

295
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:41,048
He's destroying his own
ship with his voice.

296
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:42,277
Back to work, everyone.

297
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:45,597
Let's use this to our advantage and
put some distance between us and them.

298
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:46,740
Great idea!

299
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:49,860
Look, Nami's not a demon anymore. Really?

300
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:54,220
Well, I hope she be calmer after
letting off all that steam earlier.

301
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:57,880
Luffy, we've got trouble!

302
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:00,400
This isn't good.

303
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:02,857
The waves are moving
faster than I thought.

304
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:03,940
Oh, great!

305
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:07,497
The ship's starting to break apart right
where I made all those repairs today!

306
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:08,410
Ah!

307
00:18:08,493 --> 00:18:09,986
She's beat up enough already!

308
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:13,117
If we stay here any longer,
we'll start taking on water!

309
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:14,220
Full speed ahead!

310
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:16,972
We need to get out of this voice's range!

311
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:50,117
I'm telling you, it was
the strangest thing.

312
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:51,717
This gorgeous woman walks in.

313
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:53,017
I mean, she was a knockout.

314
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:55,337
She comes up to me and leans
over the table and says,

315
00:18:55,420 --> 00:18:57,949
Tell me where this man
named Cricket lives.

316
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:01,100
Sounds like a bold woman. Bold?

317
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:03,164
No, she was more like a maniac.

318
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:04,270
All of a sudden,

319
00:19:04,353 --> 00:19:05,477
these hands started popping out from her

320
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,397
body and knocking out
everyone in the joint.

321
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,797
I'm telling you, it really
messed with my head.

322
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:10,710
Ha!

323
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:14,960
I'm confused.

324
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:18,117
What does tearing up the bar
have to do with old man Cricket?

325
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:21,777
The sea around here is the unofficial
turf of those monkey brothers.

326
00:19:21,860 --> 00:19:25,337
But if someone actually wants to have
something to do with that geezer,

327
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:28,538
then they must have caught
some of his own stupidity.

328
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:30,140
No one wants that.

329
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:35,060
I bet you what that lady's really
after is his gold. His gold?

330
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:37,281
I heard they found some recently.

331
00:19:37,820 --> 00:19:39,060
Yeah? Where at?

332
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:41,160
Hey, guys!

333
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:43,290
Bellamy!

334
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:45,940
What did you just say about gold?

335
00:19:46,820 --> 00:19:49,280
This old man that goes by crickets.

336
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:52,340
I'd like to set up a meeting with him.

337
00:19:57,820 --> 00:19:59,600
What do you know of him?
